@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).
 - **Collapse multiline statements to single-line form** (e.g., `draw_expandable_text_panel(screen, self.top, szTitle, self.X_HISTORY, self.Y_HISTORY, self.W_HISTORY, self.H_HISTORY, szText, self.bHistoryExpanded, SAS_MAGIC_PEDIA_PYTHON_HISTORY_EXPAND)`): much **easier** to **scan**, **maintain**, and **grep**, especially **for LLMs**. Often done using scripts to batch process it, and done as we go rather than all at once since this is a recent change. Especially important in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) where ~2158 lines of code have been collapsed to ~879 lines, and ~187 lines of comments to ~83 lines. See also [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md) and [PR#23](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/23). Then done in other py files in a more manual or gradual way.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5865+) **Python 2 bare-print cleanup:** converted simple active `print "..."` statements to Python 2.4/3-compatible single-string calls such as `print("msg %s" % value)`, using [`wrap_python2_prints_for_linting.py`](/LLM_Helpers/wrap_python2_prints_for_linting.py) plus manual comma-print cleanup. This keeps Civ4 Python 2.4 compatibility while reducing Ruff/Python 3 parser noise (e.g., on VS Code) so real issues are easier to see. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5880+) Also used **local ruff checks** to find and cautiously address likely fixable py linter issues that wouldn't break code changes. See [Modding_Ressources/README.md: How to check with ruff installed locally a folder](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-check-with-ruff-installed-locally-a-folder-for-py-linter-errors-candidates-to-fix-with-text-report).
-- **Repo-wide blank-line cleanup (`.py` only):** reduced excessive **consecutive blank lines** to a **single blank line** in Python files. This is a pure formatting no-op (Python ignores blank lines), but it makes large files denser, easier to scan, easier to grep, and more manageable for future review/LLM-assisted cleanup. Comments and code are untouched; only **vertical whitespace** is normalized.
+- **Repo-wide blank-line cleanup (`.py` only):** reduced excessive **consecutive blank lines** to a **single blank line** in Python files (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5887+) with a `(\r?\n)(?:[ \t]*\r?\n){2,}` find to `$1$1` regexp on VS Code. This is a pure formatting no-op (Python ignores blank lines), but it makes large files denser, easier to scan, easier to grep, and more manageable for future review/LLM-assisted cleanup. Comments and code are untouched; only **vertical whitespace** is normalized.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5885+) A later **horizontal whitespace** pass also **stripped spaces/tabs** from otherwise empty Python lines to reduce invisible diff/lint noise: done with the help of `^[\t ]+$` find regexp with replace all (to nothing) globally on VS Code.
 - Convert **single quote to double quote** (e.g. `'BONUS_IRON'` to `"BONUS_IRON"`), which allowed to **detect and fix incorrect fields** and later strengthen them with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)`.
 - **Performance & code cleanup:** Broad Python/XML/C++ optimizations (e.g., removed giant ConfigObj docstring (see [KI#21.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#215---addressed--fixed---removed-the-giant-configobj-docstring-very-inefficiently-in-the-python-code-and-commented-out-most-if-not-all-as-well)); cached hot values via `static const`/hoisting; normalized inconsistent asset names (see for example [KI#18](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#18---very-inconsistent-naming-in-some-assets))), **map-type heaviness caching** (`CvGame::recomputeMapnameHeaviness`) so land/naval checks run once per game (feeds UNITAI tuning) (see [KI#42](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#42---enhancedaddressed-tune-ais-preferred-based-unitai-based-on-war-status-offense-mode-defense-mode-combined-power-ratios-of-ennemies-etc-if-any-other-general-sanity-checks-and-efficiency-city-size-map-type-land-heavy-vs-water-heavy-vs-other-if-any-for-example-general-suicide-or-such-tendencies-etc), **bonus-specific builds/improvements caching** (e.g. `CvUnitAI::getBonusSpecificLandBuilds`), [AI Personality Panel performance optimization notes](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching)), **feature-level caching** (AI Personality Panel), refactor **extremely redundant code** (e.g. `refreshUnitSelection` in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)), cache redundant computation (e.g. **store per turn and player** top cities' values `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`), etc.

